// oxfmt configuration. JSONC rather than JSON because the values below are not
// preferences — they are a deliberate mirror of the `formatter` and
// `javascript.formatter` blocks of the biome.json this replaced, and that fact has to
// survive. oxfmt auto-discovers `.oxfmtrc.jsonc` exactly as it does `.oxfmtrc.json`.
//
// Measured before the swap, at these settings, over the same five globs `scripts/format.ts`
// hands the formatter: oxfmt disagrees with Biome on 3 of 510 files. One is a hand-laid-out
// palette that needed its suppression comment re-spelled; the other two are three-specifier
// `export … from` blocks Biome kept expanded and oxfmt collapses onto one 98-column line.
// Nothing else in the tree moved. Change any option here and that stops being true: every
// one of them is a whole-tree reflow, not a matter of taste.
//
// Per-line suppressions are spelled `// oxfmt-ignore`. oxfmt also honours
// `// prettier-ignore`, but no Prettier is involved here and a directive named after a tool
// this repo does not use is a question waiting to be asked.
//
// The directive must be the LAST comment line before the declaration it protects. Biome
// let the reason trail on the same comment block; oxfmt does not, and a directive with an
// explanation after it is silently inert — the file reformats and the comment still reads
// as though it were doing something. Put the reason above the directive, not after it.
{
  "$schema": "./node_modules/oxfmt/configuration_schema.json",
  "printWidth": 100,
  "useTabs": false,
  "tabWidth": 2,
  "semi": true,
  "singleQuote": true,
  "trailingComma": "all",
  "bracketSpacing": false,
  "arrowParens": "always",

  // A safety net, not the definition of what gets formatted: `scripts/format.ts` still hands
  // oxfmt an explicit glob list rather than the bare `oxfmt` that would suffice. Bare, oxfmt
  // reaches markdown, JSON and YAML this repo does not format, and a silently *wider* set is
  // how a generated file gets clobbered. The two defences overlap on purpose.
  "ignorePatterns": [
    "node_modules/",
    "dist/",
    ".tmp/",
    // Real workbooks and the XML pulled out of them. Formatting a fixture would change the
    // bytes a corpus case asserts against.
    "test/corpus/fixtures/",
    "pnpm-lock.yaml",
  ],
}
